izations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T03:16:48Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T03:19:29Z","body":"> No, missed it since it doesn't reference #61929. Same idea, but it decrements the counters even when its special case doesn't apply, which can give a re-added child the same cached index as the last sibling and the unstable rebuild sort can swap them. This one only touches the counters when the pop actually happens.\r\n\r\nYes, It decrement the counter in both cases because the cache will be marked as dirty if the special cases doesn't apply, which will reset the counter and re-build the cache, so there was no need for an if statement here. Thank You all, glad to see this merged.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5433915123/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]